<title>USA: Clinton names U.S. envoy to Germany.</title>
<headline>Clinton names U.S. envoy to Germany.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton on Wednesday named John Kornblum, assistant secretary of state for European and Canadian affairs, as his choice to be U.S. ambassador to Germany.</p>
<p>The nomination requires Senate confirmation. The post has been vacant since the departure of Charles Redman.</p>
